\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\qc{\loch
Figure 1. Main Inventory window illustration (Build 480 layout baseline). The required Path(s) field is the only path-input field and accepts the same per-entry syntax as toBeInventoried.txt, with multiple entries separated by semicolons. There is no separate Slam text box; use --$slam on the applicable Path(s) entry. Main action buttons are narrower, Add New Shows and Manual Tweaks use two-line labels, and button text remains centered. Corruption Handling remains a single horizontal control strip, TLOHome remains on the compact title row, and the lower output console is non-wrapping with vertical and horizontal scrollbars.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
First-run safety: Dry run performs metadata and tag planning but does not write tags, convert SHN files, rename folders, copy or delete content, or replace inventory output.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
3. Installation package and TLOHome layout}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
The release process can provide complete packages, update packages, or both for Windows onefile, Windows onedir, generic Linux, and macOS. Names follow TLO_V1.6Build<BUILD>_complete_<platform>.zip and TLO_V1.6Build<BUILD>_update_<platform>.zip. Use a complete package for a new installation. Use the exact matching update package only to refresh an existing TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
The source bundle contains the current requirements DOCX, the current RTF user manual, TLO application source, tests, and application distribution utilities. It contains no GitHub Build Process artifacts; that independently versioned process is distributed separately. Complete distributions include the current RTF user manual, FAQ, required databases, starter files, release information, checksums, and malware-scan receipts. Update distributions always omit inventory, setlists, logs, staged folders, and other user-created output. An update normally leaves TLO_DBs unchanged, but a release may explicitly include artists.sqlite and venues.txt when a database refresh is intended; the updater reports that before you apply the ZIP.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
TLOHome/\line   apps/\line     Windows/\line       tlo-ggi.exe\line       tlo-gi.exe\line       tlo-research.exe\line       tlo-reverse.exe\line       tlo-tag.exe\line       tlo-deleteDupes.cmd\line       tlo-gsi.exe\line       search-artist-db.exe\line       _internal/              Windows onedir package only\line     macOS/\line       tlo-ggi\line       tlo-gi\line       tlo-research\line       tlo-reverse\line       tlo-tag\line       tlo-deleteDupes\line       tlo-gsi\line       search-artist-db\line     Linux/\line       tlo-ggi\line       tlo-gi\line       tlo-research\line       tlo-reverse\line       tlo-tag\line       tlo-deleteDupes\line       tlo-gsi\line       search-artist-db\line   TLO_DBs/\line     artists.sqlite\line     venues.txt\line   debug/  dups/  logs/  readyForXfer/  setlists/  staged/\line   README_FIRST.txt\line   TLO-FAQ.txt\line   TLO_Inventory_User_Manual_v478.rtf\line   toBeInventoried.txt}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Every complete distribution includes tlo-gsi, tlo-research, tlo-reverse, search-artist-db, TLO_DBs/artists.sqlite, and TLO_DBs/venues.txt. The generic Linux applications are also used under WSL. The Windows onedir package places the seven PyInstaller executables directly in apps/Windows with one shared apps/Windows/_internal folder, plus tlo-deleteDupes.cmd and its private runtime; keep that folder with the executables and replace the whole apps/Windows folder when switching between onefile and onedir layouts.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Do not run inside the ZIP: Always extract the installation ZIP first. Windows and Linux cannot reliably execute the apps while dependencies, databases, or shell scripts are still compressed.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
4. Pre-installation checklist}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Choose the final TLOHome folder. Use a short absolute path such as C:\\TLOHome on Windows or $HOME/TLOHome on WSL/Linux.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Confirm that TLOHome is writable by the account that will run the apps.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Know how attached drives will be mounted. Windows runs can use drive-letter paths such as E:\\Music. WSL/Linux runs can use paths such as /mnt/e/Music after the drive is mounted and visible to that environment.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Use visible and unique volume names for search roots. They are strongly recommended, especially with external drives, backup drives, WSL paths, or drives that may get different letters over time.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- If setlist.fm lookup will be used, obtain a setlist.fm API key and set SETLISTFM_API_KEY before starting the GUI. To enable setlist.fm upgrade, also set SETLISTFMUPGRADE_API_KEY to the same API key value. If the normal key is missing, both setlist.fm controls are unchecked and greyed out. If only the upgrade variable is missing, normal setlist.fm remains available and only setlist.fm upgrade is greyed out.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Installation contents: The installation ZIP installs the application files and support folders under TLOHome. Pre-installation setup is limited to choosing a writable TLOHome location, preparing environment variables, and making sure mounted drives will be visible.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
5. Windows installation and shortcuts}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Install or refresh TLOHome}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
1.\tab Create or choose the TLOHome folder, for example C:\\TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
2.\tab Extract the installation ZIP so the apps and support folders appear inside TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
3.\tab Confirm that C:\\TLOHome\\apps\\Windows contains tlo-ggi.exe, tlo-gi.exe, tlo-research.exe, tlo-reverse.exe, tlo-tag.exe, tlo-deleteDupes.cmd, tlo-gsi.exe, and search-artist-db.exe.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
4.\tab Set the TLOHome environment variable and optional variables described in Section 7.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
5.\tab Open a new Windows terminal or restart any already-open TLO app so the changed environment is visible.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
PowerShell example:\line Expand-Archive .\\TLO_V1.6Build458_complete_Windows.zip -DestinationPath C:\\TLOHome\line setx TLOHome "C:\\TLOHome"\line setx TLOCurrentStorage "Backup-1"\line setx SETLISTFM_API_KEY "your-api-key-if-used"\line setx SETLISTFMUPGRADE_API_KEY "same-api-key-if-upgrade-is-used"}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Optional Windows shortcuts}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
After installation, you may pin tlo-ggi.exe or tlo-gsi.exe from TLOHome\\apps\\Windows to Start. Set the shortcut Start in field to TLOHome\\apps\\Windows. Windows, not TLO, controls shortcut hot keys and Startup-folder behavior.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
6. macOS, Linux, and WSL installation}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Install or refresh TLOHome}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
1.\tab Create or choose the TLOHome folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
2.\tab Extract the matching complete package, such as TLO_V1.6Build458_complete_Linux.zip or TLO_V1.6Build458_complete_macOS.zip, directly into that folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
3.\tab Use apps/macOS on macOS. Use apps/Linux on generic Linux and under WSL. There is no apps/WSL directory because WSL runs the generic Linux executables. Do not substitute a Windows or macOS build.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
4.\tab Confirm that TLOHome/TLO_DBs contains artists.sqlite and venues.txt from the complete package.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
5.\tab Set TLOHome and optional variables in the startup file used by your shell.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa0{\loch
6.\tab Use WSLg, X/Wayland, or the native macOS graphical session when launching GUI applications.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
mkdir -p "$HOME/TLOHome"\line unzip TLO_V1.6Build458_complete_Linux.zip -d "$HOME/TLOHome"\line \line cat >> ~/.profile <<'EOF'\line export TLOHome="$HOME/TLOHome"\line export TLOCurrentStorage="Backup-1"\line # export SETLISTFM_API_KEY="your-api-key-if-used"\line # export SETLISTFMUPGRADE_API_KEY="same-api-key-if-upgrade-is-used"\line EOF\line . ~/.profile\line \line # macOS\line chmod +x "$TLOHome/apps/macOS/"*\line "$TLOHome/apps/macOS/tlo-ggi"\line \line # Generic Linux or WSL\line chmod +x "$TLOHome/apps/Linux/"*\line "$TLOHome/apps/Linux/tlo-ggi"}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
WSL path entry: TLO accepts either Windows drive-letter paths or /mnt/<drive> paths in Search Path and in .txt Search Path control files. On WSL/Linux, a Windows path such as E: is normalized to /mnt/e for scanning when possible. If no bracketed volume prefix is supplied, TLO uses the mounted drive's operating-system volume label when it can resolve one.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\pagebb\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa0{\loch
7. Environment variables}
