Corruption Handling}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Grouped controls for proven corruption: Corrupt files chooses Keep and report or Delete corrupt files; Folder removal chooses Never, 100% corrupt only, or At threshold; Folder corruption threshold is 0-100. When Keep and report is selected, Folder removal is effectively Never and both folder-removal controls are greyed out. With Delete corrupt files selected, Folder removal is available and the threshold value is enabled only for At threshold. The Corrupt files drop-down is only slightly wider than the compact control and is sized to avoid clipping the end of Delete corrupt files; the Folder removal drop-down remains compact, the threshold label is single-line, and the % sign sits immediately beside the threshold value box. Defaults are Delete corrupt files and 100% corrupt only.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Corruption Handling separates folder decisions from individual-file decisions. TLO first scans the original audio population and classifies each path as healthy, proven corrupt, or unverifiable. Folder removal is evaluated first from that untouched snapshot: Never removes no folder because of corruption; 100% corrupt only removes a logical show or direct music folder only when its evaluated audio population is entirely corrupt; At threshold removes it when the proven-corruption percentage is greater than or equal to Folder corruption threshold. Only content that remains then reaches Corrupt files: Keep and report leaves proven-corrupt files in place and logs them, while Delete corrupt files moves the remaining corrupt files to the OS Trash/Recycle Bin. A failed folder Trash does not override Keep and report. Missing, locked, unreadable, disconnected, resource-failed, or validator-infrastructure-failed files are unverifiable, suppress corruption-driven Trash, and fail closed before later mutation. MP3 files are treated exactly like FLAC files for corruption handling: they are validated as audio, counted in the same corruption percentage and folder population, and follow the same Keep/Delete and Never/100%/threshold decisions.}
