Main-window checkbox controlling non-destructive Inventory, Tag, and Add Shows planning. Child windows do not have separate Dry run checkboxes.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft82\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5253\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10424\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Inventory (full)}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Shows Review Operation and then runs either the non-destructive Dry run or the full inventory using the required Search Path. There is no automatic TLOHome/toBeInventoried.txt fallback.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft82\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5253\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10424\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Pause}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Pauses full inventory between filesystem operations. Does not apply to Add Shows.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft82\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5253\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10424\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Resume}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Resumes a paused full inventory. Repeated Resume clicks report only when a pause is active.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Performance modes}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Search-path worker count is capped by the number of search paths queued for that run. Postprocess setlist/bootlist export uses a separate bounded worker pool after scanning finishes.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- gentle: best when using external drives, spinning disks, or Windows desktops where responsiveness matters. Uses 1 worker by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- balanced: moderate parallelism. GUI and CLI default performance mode. Typically uses up to 2 workers by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- fast: higher normal throughput, usually up to the CPU count by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- extreme: speed-first for inventory traversal. It may request the most parallel work, but Max Workers remains the ceiling and physical-drive, work-group, and correctness constraints may still reduce the actual worker count. Postprocess remains bounded. Extreme does not skip non-compliant tag checks.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
10. Compliant versus non-compliant mode}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Compliant mode}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Use Compliant mode when folders intentionally follow predictable naming. The main supported forms, in precedence order, are String1 Date String2, String1 - String2 Date when a complete date occurs at a String2 boundary, String1 - String2, and String1 Date. For Date, TLO first looks for yyyy-mm-dd-style dates, including legitimate partial forms such as 19xx-xx-xx and 20xx-xx-xx, same-month multi-day forms such as 1970-04-12-13 or 1970-04-12,13, and then accepted year ranges before falling back to older date-recognition rules. A same-month multi-day range may contain the first day plus one or two trailing day values; the days must be valid calendar dates and strictly ascend. Textual equivalents such as 12-13 April 1970, April 12-13, 1970, and 1970 April 12-13 are also accepted. TLO uses the first day as the canonical Date and preserves the complete original multi-day range in PARENTHETICALS. Existing year-range behavior is unchanged. Century-known 19xx/20xx partial years require the remaining month/day components to stay unknown. In compliant mode, FLAC and MP3 metadata tags are not read or used. Compliant cannot be combined with Rename Compliantly.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 Date String2: String1 is the artist text, Date is normalized, and String2 is kept as the trailing show text unless online lookup fills venue/location. By default, a matched alias is written using the Artist DB master name. Check As-Is Artist Name to preserve String1 as written.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 - String2 Date: after String1 Date String2 fails, TLO checks whether String2 begins or ends with one complete performance date. The date is normalized and assigned as Date, while the remaining String2 text stays raw as the album/show/venue tail. Example: The Georgia Satellites - Santa Cruz 01-17-87 becomes The Georgia Satellites 1987-01-17 Santa Cruz. Bare years, ranges, partial dates, and dates embedded in the middle of String2 do not trigger this refinement.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 - String2: when the boundary-date refinement does not match, String2 is treated as an album/show tail and no Date is assigned. A parenthetical-only tail such as (Live) is preserved.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Artist/Album dash spacing: once the complete leading artist text resolves uniquely in the Artist DB, the first Artist/Album dash may have spaces on both sides, one side, or neither side. Artist - Album, Artist- Album, Artist -Album, and Artist-Album are therefore equivalent only for that DB-confirmed artist boundary. Later dashes remain part of String2; arbitrary hyphens are not globally treated as separators.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Every final Show Name retains all trailing parenthetical items in their original order. TLO captures them from the original folder name before cleaning the path for artist, date, venue, and location parsing, then restores them after normalization. A recognized performance qualifier such as Early Show or Late Show is also retained as a parenthesized suffix when it is not already present. This applies to Full Inventory, Add Shows, Dry run output, folder renames, bootlist rows, setlist names, and Album tags. For example, Danny Gatton 1994-03-13 Bottom Line NYC (set 2) becomes Danny Gatton 1994-03-13 Bottom Line New York, NY (set 2).}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- String1 Date: fallback when no String2 exists; show name becomes Artist Date. Artist output follows the As-Is Artist Name checkbox.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Standard video wrapper folders such as VIDEO_TS or BDMV can resolve from parent path components.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- The Billboard MP3 year-folder special case applies only when all inventoried music files are .mp3, the folder name is a four-digit year from 1959 through 2005, and billboard appears somewhere in the path. The exported setlist filename for this special case uses the same four-digit year.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Non-compliant mode}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Use Non-compliant mode when folder names vary or contain partial or uncertain metadata. Non-compliant mode uses more evidence and tries to fill missing metadata without overwriting earlier trusted fields. As-Is Artist Name applies here too: unchecked uses an Artist DB master name for an unambiguous alias match; checked preserves the artist text from the metadata source that identified the show.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Samples ALBUMARTIST, ARTIST, ALBUM, and DATE metadata from up to two supported FLAC or MP3 files in non-compliant mode. Within the audio-tag tier, ALBUMARTIST is considered before ARTIST. Before Artist DB lookup, an explicitly dash-delimited or parenthesized terminal performance qualifier such as Early Show or Late Show is separated from a tag artist candidate. If the normal exact lookup then misses, TLO may ignore apostrophe characters for one retry, but accepts the result only when it identifies one unique Artist DB master. Tag values containing unknown or track are treated as blank for artist purposes. Artist evidence precedence is: inline --$slam; strong explicit path/folder/commercial evidence; DB-confirmed structured selected-setlist Artist metadata; DB-backed selected-setlist filename evidence; DB-matched FLAC/MP3 tag artist; and finally an unmatched raw tag artist. Structured setlist Artist metadata may replace only weak generic path/subdirectory evidence under its established confidence safeguards.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Searches folder and path text for artist, date, venue, and location clues, including known artist names and aliases. Generic path scanning does not promote an Artist DB term found entirely inside the parsed venue/location tail of a date-bearing folder; Attic inside Eddie's Attic is therefore venue text, while an exact artist directory named Attic remains eligible. Short no-space-date artist abbreviations such as gd in gd1977-05-08 are deliberately weak evidence: TLO first checks stronger tags, full DB-backed path names, selected-setlist metadata/filename evidence, and other structured sources. Only if those fail may the abbreviation resolve through artists.sqlite as a final local fallback; an enabled artist/date online lookup may corroborate it but does not promote abbreviation evidence above stronger sources.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Recognizes the non-compliant Date Artist Venue Location path pattern when a date begins the folder component. The Artist must be the longest unique Artist DB match beginning immediately after the date. A venue must remain after removing the Artist, and the remainder must also parse into City plus Region or Country. For example, 1997-04-05 Genesis Old Pub London England becomes Genesis 1997-04-05 Old Pub London, England. TLO rejects 1990-07-10 Palace Melbourne Australia under this pattern because removing Palace leaves only a location and no venue.}

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- Also recognizes a narrowly guarded non-compliant Artist + Place + Date + technical-suffix form after the ordinary path rules have had their chance. For example, if RTF is already an alias in artists.sqlite, RTF Paris 7 March 76 flac16 can resolve to Return to Forever 1976-03-07 Paris. TLO does not invent RTF from Return to Forever; the prefix itself must be a direct unique Artist DB match. The text after the date must be entirely recognizable media/source technical text such as flac16, flac24, shn, wav, 16-bit, 24-bit, SBD, AUD, FM, matrix, soundboard, or audience. State/country-anchored place text and exact venues.txt matches may be used immediately. A single unanchored word such as Paris is only a last-resort display/location hint after eTreeDB, selected setlist metadata, and setlist.fm fail to provide stronger venue/location information. Unknown multi-word text is not promoted to a place.}\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- For an ordinary non-compliant String1 - String2 name, TLO checks String2 for a complete performance date before using the generic Artist - Album fallback. It also accepts a supported partial date when that date is at the beginning or end of String2; a partial date embedded in the middle of album-like text does not force performance mode. After removing the accepted date and its surrounding dash separators, conservative venue/location parsing may establish performance metadata only when city plus state/region or country is strongly anchored and no unexplained trailing text remains. For example, Ray Price - Gilley's - Pasadena, Texas - xx-xx-81 becomes Ray Price 1981-xx-xx Gilley's Pasadena, TX. Explicit leading-year Artist - Album commercial-release forms keep their separate rules, and ambiguous album-like text remains an album rather than being forced into performance metadata.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Missing spaces around the first Artist/Album dash do not prevent album/collection identification when the complete text before that dash is a unique Artist DB match. TLO splits only that artist-delimiting dash. For example, Van Morrison-Saint Dominic's Preview-Hard Nose The Highway Live becomes Artist Van Morrison with album Saint Dominic's Preview-Hard Nose The Highway Live; the later dash stays in the album title. If the left side is unknown or ambiguous, TLO does not enable this relaxed unspaced-dash rule.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Commercial releases may use (YYYY) - Artist - Album or YYYY - Artist - Album, where YYYY is exactly one four-digit 19xx or 20xx year. TLO uses that year only to recognize the commercial-release form; it does not write the year to DATE or include it in the Show Name. Complete dates, partial dates, year ranges, two-digit years, x-filled years, and years embedded in other text do not qualify. The Show Name is Artist - Album. If the album tail already begins with the same resolved Artist followed by a dash, TLO removes that one redundant Artist component, so Rod Stewart - Rod Stewart - Camouflage becomes Rod Stewart - Camouflage. For tagging, the discovered Album portion is retained as ALBUM_NAME and is used as the base Album tag even when Date, Venue, and Location are blank; it must not fall through to Unknown.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Aggregates related wrapper/part folders such as CD1/CD2/CD3 under one logical show only when every direct music-bearing child under the parent belongs to the same release relationship. If any direct music-bearing sibling is unrelated, TLO keeps the folders separate and never promotes the broad collection/search parent into one show. A short v-number inside a larger descriptive parenthetical, such as (WLIR-FM, rm v.2), is not treated as a volume suffix. The narrow Parent/Parent (1) through Parent (N) multipart-release layout is aggregated only when all direct music-bearing children share the parent-matching base, the part numbers are consecutive from 1, and the parent itself has no direct music. Inventory discovery can continue below a recorded parent music folder so a genuinely independent nested opening act can still become its own show; normal wrapper/grouping rules prevent ordinary discs/sets from being split incorrectly.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Recognizes one additional guarded wrapper layer, such as Show/FLAC/Set 1 and Show/FLAC/Set 2. Set, Disc, Disk, CD, D, Part, Side, and Tape numbered folders may be combined under a non-numbered media container such as FLAC or Audio, and a setlist stored directly in the date-bearing Show folder applies to the complete show. TLO crosses only that validated wrapper layer and checks only files directly in the Show folder. It does not rescan sibling show folders. If unrelated music also exists below the proposed Show folder, TLO does not promote that folder into one show.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- For a date-bearing show, recognizable supplemental/source/media descendants such as Source 2 EXTRAS, Right Channel (Soundboard Feed), Open Mic Lithium, art-docs, Concert Pictures/Video, Disc 1/Flac, and Disc end tracks remain part of the dated show instead of becoming accidental independent shows. TLO keeps the descendant separate when it carries its own complete date or conflicting tagged Artist/AlbumArtist evidence, and it does not absorb a supplemental branch when another unrelated music-bearing branch such as an opening act exists below the dated show. If direct root audio and wrapper/supplemental descendants initially resolve to the same physical show root, they are collapsed into one logical group before tagging or renaming so two workers cannot independently mutate the same folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- During a real non-compliant Full Inventory, TLO can consolidate validated non-date sibling collections such as Frankie Valli - Greatest D1/D2 or Pink Floyd - Early Flights/(alt1)/(alt2) into one parent named Frankie Valli - Greatest or Pink Floyd - Early Flights. Dry Run never creates or moves this parent and blocks if an interrupted earlier consolidation requires recovery. A complete performance date excludes the rule. For this sibling-collection decision, xxxx-xx-xx is also treated as a specific date and prevents consolidation, avoiding accidental grouping of distinct unknown-date shows. A year, year span, decade label, or no year is still allowed.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- TLO compares only sibling candidates in the current search on the same partition. D/CD-style suffixes are multipart evidence. alt folders are included only when usable setlist or filename titles show materially different content; identical, overlapping, shifted, or insufficient song lists remain separate alternatives. No other partition is searched for this decision.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- TLO creates a journaled temporary sibling parent at the same level as the collection members, moves only the accepted members into it, concatenates usable member setlists into parent info.txt, and renames the completed aggregate to the shared release name. For an alt family that contains the unsuffixed base folder, Build 466 stages that original member as (alt0), so TLO creates Pink Floyd - Early Flights/Pink Floyd - Early Flights (alt0), (alt1), (alt2), and so on instead of ever creating Pink Floyd - Early Flights/Pink Floyd - Early Flights. alt0 remains first in collection-wide track order. A collision or failed operation rolls back to the exact original sibling names. Build 464 recovers the interrupted case where an older completed outer collection folder has the same pathname as one of the original member folders, and Build 465 makes that recovery portable between native Windows and WSL path forms. Existing Build 464/465 recovery journals remain supported.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
If automatic collection recovery cannot proceed safely, TLO now prints the exact recovery container, journal file, planned final folder when available, and each member's original and staged paths with its current state. ORIGINAL_ONLY and STAGED_ONLY show which side currently exists; BOTH or MISSING means TLO will not guess. Close programs that may be holding the folders open and run Inventory again. If the same error repeats, do not delete the journal or manually merge the recovery folder; preserve the listed paths for review. Dry Run remains read-only and tells you to run a normal inventory to perform automatic recovery.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- The new parent and info.txt are inventoried once; the original children remain intact beneath it. Files are ordered one child at a time, including layouts such as D1/FLAC and D2/FLAC, and tagged with one continuous 01-N sequence, or 001-N when there are more than 99 tracks.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Uses selected setlist header metadata for date, artist, venue, and location fallback before track names or hash/checksum sections. Supported strong header shapes include strict unlabeled Artist / Venue, City, State-or-Country / Date; compact Artist Date and Artist Date Venue lines where the date anchors the split; concise Location -- Venue or Venue -- Location; and Artist followed by Live at Venue, City, State/Region/Country, Date. Introductory prose cannot shift the Artist/Venue slots, and a trailing performance date on a Live at line is removed before Venue/Location splitting. Before Artist DB lookup, an explicitly separated terminal performance qualifier is removed from the structured artist candidate, and the same unique-only apostrophe retry used for tag artists is available after an exact miss. An unlabeled or compact artist is accepted only when it resolves uniquely in artists.sqlite. A DB-confirmed structured setlist artist may correct a conflicting artist supported only by weaker generic path/subdirectory scanning, but it does not override $slam or strong explicit commercial/folder artist evidence. Structured selected-setlist Artist metadata is evaluated before selected-setlist-filename and FLAC/MP3 tag artist evidence. A single-word Artist DB hit embedded in a selected-setlist filename is accepted only when the filename has strong positional structure, such as the date being the first substantive component after the artist. Location parsing requires the state/region/country to terminate the location expression, rejects title-like city fragments ending in connectives such as In, At, On, Of, To, or From, accepts safe mixed-case state codes only in strongly delimited forms, and avoids pulling very short venue words out of unrelated longer lines or comma-separated performer lists. A date followed by a double-dash duration remains valid date evidence. Ordinary text sampling is bounded to 1 MiB, full ordinary-text reads above 16 MiB are rejected, and DOCX document.xml content above 16 MiB uncompressed is rejected before decompression.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
- Artist DB terminal-suffix fallback is guarded. TLO queries the complete candidate first. Only after a complete-name miss may it strip one terminal Band, Group, All Star/All-Star/All Stars/All-Stars, or the corresponding ... Band form and retry. The shorter name must resolve uniquely and nonterminal occurrences are never stripped. When that fallback succeeds, TLO restores the exact removed suffix for the performance artist unless the DB master already ends in a supported grouping suffix. Restored performance names that are not themselves full Artist DB masters are added to TLOHome/artistsNotInDatabase.txt for review.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Uses eTreeDB and setlist.fm only when enabled, and only to fill blanks or report observations.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Commas in unnumbered song lists do not need to be followed by spaces; TLO treats \u8220\'93Song A,Song B,Song C\u8221\'94 the same as \u8220\'93Song A, Song B, Song C\u8221\'94 when the item count matches the audio files.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8640\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Practical choice: When in doubt, start with non-compliant mode for mixed real-world collections. Use compliant mode when you deliberately organized the folders to match the supported naming patterns and want those names trusted.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
11. Online lookup options}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa80{\loch
Online lookup is optional. It is used to fill missing venue/location fields after artist and a full yyyy-mm-dd date are known. Normally, later sources do not overwrite nonblank metadata found earlier. In non-compliant mode, one narrow correction is allowed: higher-confidence selected-setlist venue/location metadata may replace a conflicting value supported only by weaker path-part evidence. eTreeDB and other stronger evidence are not displaced. Other non-equivalent disagreements are reported as observations in the summary log.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- etreeDB checkbox or --etree-lookup: uses eTreeDB first among online sources. When tagging is enabled, the same option can also allow a last-resort eTreeDB song-title lookup if local setlist titles are not usable.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- setlist.fm checkbox or --setlistfm-lookup: in normal matching, uses setlist.fm as a last resort when etreeDB does not return usable venue/location data. On the command line, --setlistfm-lookup requires --etree-lookup. In the GUI, selecting setlist.fm automatically selects etreeDB. When Thorough Setlist Matching is enabled, setlist.fm becomes a proactive evidence source when enabled: TLO may query it even after etreeDB succeeds and may collect additional same-date candidates so they can corroborate or challenge the local/eTree setlist. This broader coverage does not give setlist.fm higher authority.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- setlist.fm requires SETLISTFM_API_KEY in the environment. setlist.fm upgrade additionally requires SETLISTFMUPGRADE_API_KEY, set to the same key value.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- Normal setlist.fm access is rate-limited to one request every 600 milliseconds across local workers and capped at 1,400 calls per inventory run. If both setlist.fm and setlist.fm upgrade are checked, TLO instead permits up to 14 requests per second and enforces a shared maximum of 48,000 requests per UTC day across TLO runs using the same TLOHome. Thorough Setlist Matching does not raise these limits by itself: with setlist.fm enabled but upgrade off, better coverage can take substantially longer and may be curtailed by the normal rate/run limits. With upgrade on, Thorough uses the same deconfliction rules but can gather setlist.fm evidence much more aggressively. Upgrade changes coverage/capacity, never setlist.fm authority. Coordination state is stored under TLOHome/logs/setlistfm-state rather than the system temporary directory. If a worker cannot acquire the reservation lock within 20 seconds, TLO records the lookup failure and continues without waiting indefinitely.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40{\loch
- For U.S. lookup results, show names use Artist Date Venue City StateCode. Non-U.S. results use Artist Date Venue City Country.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
Thorough Setlist Matching}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Thorough Setlist Matching is a separate accuracy-versus-time choice. It defaults off. With it off, TLO preserves early stopping and the familiar local setlist, eTreeDB, then setlist.fm fallback behavior. With it on, TLO continues gathering reasonable local candidates plus whichever online lookup sources are enabled; etreeDB is included only when etreeDB is checked, and setlist.fm only when setlist.fm is checked. In the main-window Info area, Thorough itself produces no extra message when neither online source is selected; when online sources are selected, the message names only those enabled sources. TLO compares exact-count and near-count (plus or minus two) lists, uses filename and existing Title-tag corroboration, Venue/Location compatibility, and independent-source agreement, and can align recording-only Intro/Tuning/Crowd items or performance-only Encore items without shifting every later track. A strong recording-local list can still beat online consensus when the actual audio supports it; matching eTreeDB and setlist.fm data can beat a weak local parse. If the best two cross-source candidates are nearly tied but materially different, TLO reports an ambiguity rather than silently choosing by precedence.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
When setlist.fm is enabled, Thorough makes setlist.fm proactive even after a usable eTreeDB answer and can inspect additional same-date results. This can take substantially longer under normal setlist.fm access because the ordinary 600-millisecond spacing and 1,400-call run cap still apply. setlist.fm upgrade removes that major coverage/time constraint by allowing the existing upgraded 14-requests-per-second / 48,000-per-UTC-day capacity. Upgrade affects accessibility and coverage only; it never gives setlist.fm greater authority in the final decision.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Command-line equivalent: --thorough-setlist-matching.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
Command-line rule: --compliant and --rename-compliantly cannot be used together; TLO reports an argument error.\line Command-line examples:\line tlo-gi.exe --TLOHome C:\\TLOHome --etree-lookup\line python3 tlo-gi.py --TLOHome "$TLOHome" --compliant --as-is-artist-name --etree-lookup --setlistfm-lookup}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1{\loch
12. Tagging functions}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Use the Tag button on the main Inventory window when you want TLO to write tags to audio files without running a full inventory. Build 469 no longer opens a separate Tag window. GUI Tag uses the master Path(s), including inline --$slam directives, the selected Tag in Place / Tag Copy / Tag Copy/Delete Original mode, and all current main-window lookup, corruption, tagging, Dry run, Performance Mode, and Max Workers settings. Progress and output stay in the main window. The standalone tlo-tag command-line application remains available for direct command-line tagging.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\qc{

}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\qc{\loch\fs18\i\loch
}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
GUI Tag runs directly from the main Inventory window. It uses every parsed master Path(s) job, including any inline --$slam directive, and current main-window settings. Select Tag in Place, Tag Copy, or Tag Copy/Delete Original before clicking Tag. Tag Copy and Tag Copy/Delete Original use the same destination prompt, capacity checks, verification, and source-retention/removal safeguards as Inventory. FLAC and MP3 are both first-class taggable formats and use the same metadata/title/track assignment flow. Corruption is assessed before mutation with the same fail-closed rules as Inventory. When Dry run is selected, Tag resolves metadata, track titles, copy/move/rename plans, and SHN conversion targets without changing files. The main Current Operation panel, Pause/Resume controls, output console, and completion summary are reused for Tag. Standalone tlo-tag remains available and tags its command-line tag path directly.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Before an actual tag save, TLO compares the exact normalized Artist, Album, Title, and Track Number it intends to write with the current file. With Delete extra tags unchecked, when those values already match and no stale TRACKTOTAL, DISCNUMBER, or DISCTOTAL metadata needs removal, the file is reported unchanged and is not rewritten; unrelated existing metadata is preserved. With Delete extra tags checked, TLO clears tag metadata and writes back only Artist, Album, Track Number, and Title, removing Album Artist, date/year, genre, comments, encoder fields, disc/total fields, and embedded tag artwork where supported. In that mode, a file is unchanged only when the four retained fields already match and there is no other tag metadata or artwork to remove. Rename Compliantly uses the same no-op principle, but exact spelling and capitalization are significant: Full Inventory, Add Shows, GUI Tag, and standalone tlo-tag skip the filesystem rename only when the final compliant folder name exactly matches the current name. A capitalization-only difference, such as dave van ronk becoming Dave Van Ronk after Artist DB normalization, is a real rename. On case-insensitive filesystems TLO applies such a change through a unique temporary sibling and then the exact compliant name, so the case change is recorded without creating an alternate/copy suffix.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Standalone tlo-tag does not copy or move show folders; its only source-file replacement is verified Convert shn. GUI Tag follows the selected main tag mode: Tag in Place mutates the source, Tag Copy creates and verifies a separate copy, and Tag Copy/Delete Original safely moves or verified-copies the show before removing the source. Failed SHN conversions leave the source file in place.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
On native Windows installations, GUI Tag uses the same main Path(s) drag-and-drop behavior as Inventory. Multiple dropped folders or .txt control files are appended under the normal Path(s) rules. There is no separate GUI Tagging Path field.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1{\loch
Track-title safety: when a numbered setlist begins with a bare track number such as 01 and the next meaningful numbered song row confirms 02, TLO keeps track 01 with Title Unknown and continues the numbered list. A short numeric-only row cannot start an unstructured unnumbered-title block; numeric song names such as 69 and 1999 remain valid when embedded inside an established song block. Compact personnel credits such as Gary Burton(vib) or Chick Corea (p), and duration summaries such as min 38:24 are not unnumbered song titles. A convincing run of at least three consecutive numbered song rows still blocks arbitrary later prose from being scavenged merely because its line count matches the audio files. Before a shorter numbered candidate is padded with Unknown titles, however, TLO now checks for a plausible unnumbered song-list candidate whose count exactly matches the audio files. If numbered and unnumbered candidates both match the audio count, matching audio filenames and existing Title tags only reinforce a candidate; missing or unrelated filename/tag values are neutral. A short numbered block embedded in surrounding collector prose may lose an otherwise unsupported equal-count tie to a contiguous unnumbered song block. For an explicit Setlist:, Songs:, or Tracks: section containing one song per line, Notes: and other track-list terminators end the song section before later numbered collector notes can be interpreted as tracks. Legitimate titles beginning with Thank remain valid; prose such as Thanks to the taper remains a terminator. E:, Enc:, and Encore: prefixes are removed from an encore song title. Multi-disc filenames that include both disc and track tokens, including punctuation-separated forms such as CJM-Disc01,Track01.flac, are ordered by disc first and track second so disc 1 completes before disc 2 and written Track Number tags do not alternate odd/even between discs. The same ordering applies to validated multipart release folders named Parent (1) through Parent (N): the parenthesized part number is ordered first and each folder's filename track number second, so part 1 completes before part 2 and written Track Number tags do not stripe all track 01 files across the parts. Explicit Set 1, Disc 1, Disk 1, CD 1, Setlist 1, Set List 1, Track List 1, Songs:, and Tracks: headings mark the beginning of an unnumbered song region. When one is present, artist/venue/lineage text above the first boundary is not eligible as song titles just because adding those lines would make the count match the audio files. Blank lines, later Set/Disc/Disk/CD boundaries, and a bare Encore heading can continue the same ordered region. A date-labelled filler divider such as on July 7, 1967: is skipped as a title while following songs remain eligible. Notes/source/checksum/technical markers and decorative separators end the region. Valid date-prefixed broadcast/show dividers with trailing context, for example 30.10.1948 - Royal Roost, NY - WMCA Radio broadcast, are section boundaries and are not track 30. In an established numbered run, if TLO provisionally sees a higher number but the next numbered row resumes the exact number that was expected, the higher row is discarded as a false positive; 01-07, a date-like 30 row, then 08 therefore continues with track 08. Confirmed large gaps remain valid when later numbering reinforces them, such as 01, 02, 30, 31. Artist/header safety: a DB artist word embedded only as the trailing city of a longer path location such as Washington, DC is not used as generic path artist evidence, although an exact artist directory named Washington remains valid. Structured unlabeled headers may contain Artist / room-or-hall / named Venue / Location / Date; TLO keeps the first line as artist and the deeper named venue as Venue. A collaboration such as Chick Corea and Herbie Hancock may be accepted without a combined Artist DB row only when every component resolves uniquely in the Artist DB. Bare-number title safety: when one contiguous bare-number block exactly matches the audio-file count, the numbers are treated as track positions and the Titles are Unknown; the numeric values themselves are never written as song titles.\line The tagger also creates CorruptFlacs.txt in TLOHome. If a FLAC or MP3 file cannot be opened or written during tagging, TLO appends the complete file path to that file so bad audio files can be reviewed separately from other tagging errors. The historical filename is retained for compatibility. Exact placeholder titles Title, Titled, or Titles become Unknown after normal cleanup, including numbered forms such as 01. Title; longer legitimate titles containing those words are left unchanged. Machine-generated extraction/analysis tables are never accepted as song lists merely because their rows form a clean numeric sequence. Exact Audio Copy (EAC) TOC/extraction rows and other timestamp/sector-style multi-column records are technical data, and EAC markers start a technical tail that is not mined for titles. An explicit Songs: or Tracks: block is still retained as real local list evidence even when its count differs from the audio-file count; TLO reports the mismatch instead of truncating, shifting, or inventing a one-to-one mapping. When an apostrophe-style duration is accidentally joined to a valid dated subsection heading because of a lost newline, TLO can retain the song row while removing the attached dated-divider text.}
